// register tier one's chrome uses (src/i18n.js): الميزان for the escapement,
// شوكة الميزان for the pallet fork, عجلة التوازن for the balance, النابض
// الشعري for the hairspring, الفيوزي for the fusee (no Arabic word exists;
// the transliteration is the trade's), التعبئة for winding, الميناء for the
// dial. One movement cannot have two names for a part.
//
// THE FIRST RIGHT-TO-LEFT TABLE, and the strings here do not know it: the
// mirroring is the document's (LOCALES' `dir`, src/i18n.js), the plates keep
// direction: ltr so their text anchors stay where they were drawn, and an
// Arabic run inside an ltr plate label shapes and orders itself. What a
// translator DOES decide is the arrows in link text — a back link points
// right in a right-to-left header, so ← became →.
//
// NUMBERS ARE NOT LOCALIZED ON THIS PAGE and they are WESTERN DIGITS: the
// constants are quoted from src/*.js, so 0.15 is 0.15 here as in every other
// table, never ٠٫١٥ — tools/explain-i18n.mjs compares the digit glyphs byte
// for byte, and an Arabic-Indic digit is simply not a number to it. Emphasis
// the English carries as CAPITALS rides the wording (بالفعل، إنما، fronting),
// never an added <em> — the markup gate compares tag sequences per key.
//
// "مُنمذَج" vs "مُحاكى" tracks the repo's modelled/simulated distinction
// exactly: مُنمذَج = described, مُحاكى = driven by causality.
